                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "After playing through this again, I still like the game and it fits the original very well but bigger. The main issue is that they didn't fix the gameplay issues from the first, the controls are clunky, the puzzles can be confusing and need to be done in a specific order, and combat is underwhelming. The combat in this game is much more invasive than the first and it feels off, I'm not a huge fan of the energy system especially when running out stops jumping as well. In the original there were puzzles that felt a bit stupid and this one has more of those just because it is bigger which means there is more time that you spend just wandering trying to figure something out. \n\nNow, after those issues I still recommend this game for the same reason the first one is so great; Story. The story is this one I personally don't enjoy as much as the original but it still gives that itch that leaves you wanting more, I wish the gameplay was a little smoother because the story is so compelling and the twists always hit their mark.",
